@@ Module for unit aware range commands.
@@ At the time of writing, 2025-09-03, the db48x range commands are not unit aware.
@@ This is not production ready but a db48x rpl programming exercise.
@@ Inspired by https://github.com/c3d/db48x/issues/1522

'RangeWithUnits' CreateDirectory
RangeWithUnits


«
	@@ Create a range from an a and b value with units, given a range command.
	@@ The unit of the a value is ignored.
	@@ The unit of the b value is used as the unit for the range.
	@@
	@@ (a_aUnit b_bUnit RangeCommand -- <a b range>_rangeUnit)

	→ RangeCommand
        «
		@ Ignore aUnit, remove it.
		Swap Object→ Drop Swap
		@ (-- a b_bUnit)

		@ Preserve bUnit. Later attach it to the range.
		1 Over →Unit UnRot
		@ (-- 1_bUnit a b_bUnit)

		@ Remove bUnit.
		Object→ Drop
		@ (-- 1_bUnit a b)

		@ Create the range. Attach the unit.
		RangeCommand Run
		Swap →Unit
		@ (-- <a b range>_rangeUnit)
	»
»
'RangeWithUnitsWrapper' Store	


@@ With the above wrapper, the different range commands are easily created.
@@ Providing one as an example.
«
	'→σRange' RangeWithUnitsWrapper
»
'→σRangeWithUnits' Store


«
	@@ Break up a range with units to its a and b value, with units.
	@@ (<a b range>_rangeUnit -- a_aUnit b_bUnit)

	@ Preserve the rangeUnit. Later attach it to a and b.
	1 Over →Unit Swap
	@ (-- 1_rangeUnit <a b range>_rangeUnit)

	@ Remove the rangeUnit. Break up the range.
	Object→ Drop Object→
	@ (-- 1_rangeUnit a b)

	@ Attach unit to b.
	Pick3 →Unit
	@ (-- 1_rangeUnit a b_bUnit)
	
	@ Attach unit to a.
	UnRot Swap →Unit Swap
	@ (-- a_aUnit b_bUnit)
»
'RangeWithUnits→' Store


«
	@@ Scientific round an uncertain number with a unit.
	@@ (<mean>±σ<standardDeviation>_unit -- <mean rounded>±σ<standardDeviation rounded>_unit)

	@ Breakup the uncertain number.
	RangeWithUnits→
	@ (-- mean_unit standardDeviation_unit)
	
	@ Round the standardDeviation.
	-2 round
	@ Round the mean accordingly.
	dup unrot StandardRound Swap
	@ (--  <mean rounded>_unit <standardDeviation rounded>_unit)

	@ Rebuild the uncertain number.
	→σRangeWithUnits
	@ (--  <mean rounded>±σ<standardDeviation rounded>_unit)
»
'ScientificRoundUncertainNumberWithUnits' Store


@@ Provide easy access with a custom menu.
@@ Note the difference in "→σRange" and the 3 before it.
@@ That makes the "→σRange" button work even when in programming mode.
@@ The 3 before it get run immediately even in programming mode.
{
	{ "→Range" « '→Range' RangeWithUnitsWrapper » }
	{ "→∆Range" « '→∆Range' RangeWithUnitsWrapper » }
	{ "→%Range" « '→%Range' RangeWithUnitsWrapper » }
	{ "→σRange" →σRangeWithUnits }
	{ "Range→" RangeWithUnits→ }
	{ "SciRnd" ScientificRoundUncertainNumberWithUnits }
}
'CustomMenu' STO


